// S5 -- "Gause's jar", `Reports/lab-behaviour-scenarios-2026-09-06.md`.
// A pure `labbatch` sweep -- the bed (its `compartments`) is the whole
// experiment, and neither the founders nor the colonies carry any hand
// placement of their own. In one open compartment a beetle population
// historically either eats the colony down and starves out, or never finds
// enough of it to persist; walled into four, a room the beetles have not
// found yet is a refuge for both sides. Gause's classic prediction (spatial
// structure extends coexistence) gives the instrument a textbook answer to
// check itself against.
//
// `compartments` is exactly what `labbatch scenario=gauses_jar
// sweep=compartments values=1,4,16` sweeps -- `params::write_bed` already
// names it, so this file supplies nothing but the base bed a sweep varies
// one field of.
//
// **The colony and the beetles arrive on the timeline, not at build time.**
// `labshot scenario=gauses_jar frames=0,100,1200` used to read `plants 0`
// from frame 100 on: `bed.colonies=4, bed.colony_ants=26, bed.predators=4`
// founded four colonies of 26 ants beside the eight herb founders on frame
// 0, and the ants ate every seedling before any of them grew past a
// founder. So the bed founds no colony and releases no beetle of its own
// (`colonies: 0, predators: 0`, `founders: 8` unchanged) and the timeline
// gives the plants a 3,000-frame head start: `Colonies(ant, 4, 26)` at
// frame 3,000 founds one colony per compartment exactly where
// `LabBox::colony_columns()` would put them for `colonies: 4` (so a
// `compartments` sweep still lands one colony per room at 1, 4 or 16), and
// `Predators(beetle, 4)` follows at frame 6,000 the same way over
// `predator_columns()`. `compartments` and `colony_ants` are otherwise
// untouched, so the sweep this file exists for still sweeps the same bed.
(
    name: "gauses_jar",
    title: "GAUSE'S JAR",
    question: "Swept over compartments 1, 4, 16 -- does walling the jar extend how long both the colony and the beetles persist?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 96,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 4,
        founders: 8,
        species: "herb",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 26,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [],
    timeline: [
        (at: 3000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colonies(species: "ant", colonies: 4, ants: 26)),
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Predators(species: "beetle", count: 4)),
    ],
    horizon: 60000,
)
